<LLMTokenQuota name="LTQ-Count" continueOnError="true" enabled="true">
  <DisplayName>LLM Token Quota (count)</DisplayName>
  <!--
    Records what a call actually consumed, against the department's budget.
    LTQ-Enforce checks the counter in the request flow and adds nothing; this
    adds the real figure in the response flow, because the token count does not
    exist until the model has answered.

    USAGE SOURCE CHANGED 2026-09-15, twice over, and both changes matter.

    1. It now reads a flow variable instead of an inline message template. The
       previous value was
         {jsonPath($.usageMetadata.candidatesTokenCount,response.content,true)}
       which is the same message-template jsonPath() mechanism PROVEN not to
       work against the Vertex response body in a debug session that same day
       (see EV-TokenUsage.xml and apigee/disabled/model-armor/EV-ModelResponseText.xml).
       If it never resolved, this policy has been counting ZERO on every call
       and the department budget has never moved. A quota that never fills is
       indistinguishable from a quota that is never reached, so nothing would
       have signalled it. EV-TokenUsage now does the extraction with
       ExtractVariables, which demonstrably works in this proxy.

    2. It now counts TOTAL tokens, not output tokens. candidatesTokenCount is
       output only: on a measured Translation job that was 87,510 of 415,000,
       about 21% of real consumption, ignoring the larger and still billed half.
       This moved together with the product's llmQuota value, because changing
       the basis alone silently revalues the limit by roughly 5x.

    continueOnError stays true: a counting failure must not fail a call the
    model already answered and that is already billed. The cost of that choice
    is that a broken extraction degrades to counting zero rather than erroring,
    which is exactly point 1 above. VERIFY against an application's own recorded
    token total before trusting this counter.
  -->
  <Operation>CountOnly</Operation>
  <UseQuotaConfigInAPIProduct stepName="VA-ApiKey"/>
  <Identifier ref="llm_user_department"/>
  <LLMTokenUsageSource>{llm.total_tokens}</LLMTokenUsageSource>
  <LLMModelSource>{llm.model}</LLMModelSource>
</LLMTokenQuota>
